{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:18.255.090","page_type":"section"},"citation":"18.255.090","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.255.090","content_hash":"2159d791b2a79a2e808fea75154ed482d868bcd4ac7b85c5c27ceb5f109f0583","heading":"Design review guidelines.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.255.090:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.255.090","text":"(a) Design review guidelines for each local historic district shall address the following:\n(1) Acceptable materials for any construction, additions, remodeling or rehabilitation activities to the exterior of the structures;\n(2) Appropriate architectural character, scale, and detail for any construction, additions, remodeling or rehabilitation activities;\n(3) Acceptable appurtenances to the structures;\n(4) Acceptable textures and ornamentation to the exterior of the structures;\n(5) Acceptable accessories on structures;\n(6) Such other building regulations which would have impact on the buildings;\n(7) Acceptable standards for changes to noncontributing resources within the district; and\n(8) Acceptable signage.\n(b) The Topeka Landmarks Commission shall make available the proposed design review guidelines to each owner of record in a proposed local historic district prior to consideration by the Commission. (Ord. 19901 § 10, 5-6-14.)","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"2501fabc-feac-592a-b673-feb365d5c310"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"18.255.090","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.255.090","content_hash":"f060794417b295c123a87896ba9f43d57d4a1c1fb5c36d502e6277c78cc8fb33","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tm